cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "VIMERA: A reproducible framework for synthetic virome benchmarking and empirical assessment of viral detection"
message: "If you use VIMERA, please cite the manuscript in preparation and credit the VIMERA authors."
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Gonzalez
    given-names: Gabriel

version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-11

repository-code: "https://github.com/PLACEHOLDER/VIMERA"

abstract: >
  VIMERA is a reproducible framework for benchmarking viral metagenomics
  pipelines through controlled synthetic virome generation and empirical
  assessment of viral detection in real sequencing datasets. The framework
  integrates taxonomy-aware genome selection, established sequencing
  simulators, read-level ground truth, empirical null distributions,
  controlled spike-in experiments, and detection performance assessment.

keywords:
  - viral metagenomics
  - viromics
  - bioinformatics
  - benchmarking
  - virus detection
  - synthetic metagenomics
  - sequencing simulation
  - taxonomy
  - reproducibility

